+## 5. Defects found and fixed (all inside the DOC-14 acceptance scope)
+
+### Defect 1 — S3 credential precedence inverted (docs/guide/configuration.md, DOC-13 rows)
+- Doc claimed `DUCKBRAIN_S3_*` is primary and "falls back to `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` if unset".
+- Source truth: `src/s3/query.ts:104-113` — `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID ?? DUCKBRAIN_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID`
+  (the comment on line 104 calls the AWS-first order "the pre-existing precedence, unchanged";
+  the file header at lines 12-14 lists direct env with AWS first).
+- Fix: both rows now state `AWS_* > DUCKBRAIN_S3_*`.
+
+### Defect 2 — stale synthetic git identity fallback (docs/guide/configuration.md, 3 lines)
+- Doc claimed (example config line 46, settings table line 73, Git User Configuration
+  line 252) that author identity falls back to `duckbrain@localhost.localdomain`.
+- Source truth: `src/config/index.ts:75-79` — `authorEmail` is optional with NO default
+  and a GIT-IDENTITY-001 comment pointing at the git identity chain;
+  `src/git/identity.ts` (whole module) removed the synthetic identity and
+  `requireGitIdentity`/`resolveAuthorEmail` THROW with an actionable setup hint when
+  nothing resolves. `initializeConfig` (the only writer of that default shape) has zero
+  callers. The old text also contradicted the DOC-13 rows in the same file.
+- Fix: example shows a placeholder (`you@example.com`), the table row marks the field
+  optional and not consulted at runtime, and the Git User Configuration section now
+  states the real resolution order and the loud failure.
+
+### Defect 3 — `--help` global-option claim too broad (docs/guide/cli-reference.md, DOC-12)
+- Doc's Global options table claimed `--help, -h` works "for the command".
+- Live truth: `remember --help`, `service --help`, `search-index --help` reject the
+  flag and print their usage with the valid flag list instead.
+- Fix: the row now names the nuance.
